  <title>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">Building the MHPSS-Gender-Peacebuilding Nexus: Fostering Wellbeing, Non-violent, Gender Equitable Masculinity, and Social Restoration with Young People in West Darfur, Sudan</narrative>
  </title>
  <description>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">This pilot project focuses on a crucial integration of capacity building for mental health and psychosocial support services (MHPSS) for the community in West Darfur, Sudan, especially the youth, to address the cycles of conflict and trauma, while supporting community and youth-led programmes to address the root causes of conflict, promote peacebuilding, social cohesion, and improve gender relations including notions of masculinity. This is accomplished by supporting the Ministry of Health to provide comprehensive MHPSS services and encouraging the community, especially the youth who have been impacted by conflict, to seek out these services. The project promotes peace education and provides guidance and material support to youth groups to work together within their own communities to address gender issues, peacebuilding, governance, rule of law, justice, and socio-economic recovery in an effort to contribute to ending the cycle of conflict.</narrative>
  </description>
